From: MCC45TR <mcc45tr@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: compare O82 active-video DMA frame blocking

Uke MiCode display 44275c404a677d9d9e5230fedd1af2ef02fc7b9a,
msm/dsi/dsi_ctrl_hw_cmn.c (GPL-2.0-only), and the working O82 controller
capture leave TRIG_CTRL bit12 clear. Same-SoC OnePlus SM7675 modules/DT
1138e00fee63582a0cc6a53af3286621786827b7 uses the same trigger policy.
Upstream sets this legacy block for all 6G>=1.2 hosts. Compare its exclusion
only on powered/enabled exact O82 initial120 transfers, after link clocks
are enabled and before command-engine enable. Preserve every other trigger
bit, scheduling, rates, IRQ masks, packet and DMA quarantine. This remains
an isolated optical experiment, not a general host fix or proven cause.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -2702,6 +2702,15 @@
 		cfg_hnd->ops->link_clk_set_rate(msm_host);
 	cfg_hnd->ops->link_clk_enable(msm_host);
 
+	/* Exact OEM video transfers leave the legacy within-frame DMA block clear. */
+	if (msm_host->enabled && dsi_uke_o82_initial120(msm_host)) {
+		u32 trigger = dsi_read(msm_host, REG_DSI_TRIG_CTRL);
+
+		if (trigger & DSI_TRIG_CTRL_BLOCK_DMA_WITHIN_FRAME)
+			dsi_write(msm_host, REG_DSI_TRIG_CTRL,
+				  trigger & ~DSI_TRIG_CTRL_BLOCK_DMA_WITHIN_FRAME);
+	}
+
 	/* TODO: vote for bus bandwidth */
 
 	if (!(msg->flags & MIPI_DSI_MSG_USE_LPM))
